<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Deployments — DKIM2</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Who runs DKIM2 on real mail today, and the software that supports it.">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../style.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="../nav.css">
</head>
<body>
  <nav class="site"><a class="brand" href="../">DKIM2</a> <span class="links"><a href="../how/">How it works</a> <a href="../get-ready/">Get ready</a> <a href="../try/">Try it</a> <a href="../implementations/">Implementations</a> <a href="../developers/">Developers</a> <a href="../deployments/" aria-current="page">Deployments</a> <a href="../verify/">Verify</a></span></nav>
  <header class="hero page">
    <h1>Deployments</h1>
    <p class="lede">Who runs DKIM2 on real mail today, and the software that
      supports it.</p>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section id="services">
      <h2>Services running DKIM2</h2>
      <p>A &#x2713; under <strong>Verifies</strong> means the service checks
        DKIM2 on incoming mail and records the result; it need not act on it
        yet. The date links to a public statement where there is one;
        &ldquo;reported to us&rdquo; means the operator told us directly.</p>
      <div class="table-scroll">
  <!-- SITES -->
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="software">
      <h2>Supporting software</h2>
      <p>Mail servers and MTAs you can run yourself that sign or verify DKIM2.
        For libraries, test tools and hosted checkers, see
        <a href="../implementations/">Implementations</a>.</p>
      <div class="table-scroll">
  <!-- SOFTWARE -->
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="add">
      <h2>Add yours</h2>
      <p>Running DKIM2 in production, or shipping it? Open a pull request
        adding a file under <code>deploy/www/deployments/sites/</code> or
        <code>software/</code> (copy an existing one) at
        <a href="https://github.com/dkim2wg/interop">github.com/dkim2wg/interop</a>,
        or tell us there.</p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <p>DKIM2 · developed in the IETF DKIM working group · 2026</p>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
